WEBVTT

00:27:57.798 --> 00:28:00.950
They can showcase the candidates'
skills and values in real time,

00:28:00.974 --> 00:28:02.130
in a concrete way

00:28:02.154 --> 00:28:04.804
that structured interviews
and most algorithms can't.

00:28:05.661 --> 00:28:08.888
Dave Chang has been gathering
work samples for years.

00:28:08.912 --> 00:28:11.268
When he interviews candidates
for restaurant jobs,

00:28:11.292 --> 00:28:12.615
he asks them to cook.

00:28:13.303 --> 00:28:14.847
DC: Make an omelet.

00:28:14.871 --> 00:28:16.892
Because I want to see
what they care about,

00:28:16.916 --> 00:28:18.555
and how they do something.

00:28:18.579 --> 00:28:20.414
You can tell a lot about an individual

00:28:20.438 --> 00:28:21.795
if they're cracking the eggs

00:28:21.819 --> 00:28:24.779
and then trying to get every bit
of the albumen out of the egg.

00:28:24.803 --> 00:28:26.138
How organized are they?

00:28:26.162 --> 00:28:28.480
So I'm not trying to see
perfect technique,

00:28:28.504 --> 00:28:30.827
I'm trying to see
the intent of the individual,